<item><title>Mali dismantles Bamako site as 487 expelled from Guinea await return</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-dismantles-bamako-site-as-487-expelled-from-guinea-e34211/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-dismantles-bamako-site-as-487-expelled-from-guinea-e34211/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>Authorities have moved 467 people to a Ouinzindougou hostel while 20 Burkinabè remain at Kouremalé, pending return arrangements with their governments.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:58:03 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" length="29829" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mali’s army frees 24 detained soldiers near Kidal</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-s-army-frees-24-detained-soldiers-near-kidal-9d251a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-s-army-frees-24-detained-soldiers-near-kidal-9d251a/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>The soldiers were taken to Gao after a coordinated operation by the army and its partners in In-Tebezas on Wednesday.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:58:40 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-s-army-frees-24-detained-soldiers-near-kidal-9d251a/share.jpg" length="37764" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-s-army-frees-24-detained-soldiers-near-kidal-9d251a/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mali diabetes care burdens patients with travel and food costs</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-diabetes-care-burdens-patients-with-travel-and-food-66ce47/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/mali-diabetes-care-burdens-patients-with-travel-and-food-66ce47/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>Patients face expenses beyond medicines and consultations, while official figures estimate 350 000 to 700 000 people live with diabetes in Mali.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:39:52 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" length="29829" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Koutiala workshop tackles land and herder disputes in San and Koutiala</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/koutiala-workshop-tackles-land-and-herder-disputes-in-san-72ac20/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/koutiala-workshop-tackles-land-and-herder-disputes-in-san-72ac20/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>The workshop, held in Koutiala in Mali&apos;s south, focused on preventing violence over natural resources and climate change in San and Koutiala.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:27:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" length="29829" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Malian youth group gets about 20 participants to pay local tax</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/malian-youth-group-gets-about-20-participants-to-pay-local-7d7d1d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ml/malian-youth-group-gets-about-20-participants-to-pay-local-7d7d1d/</guid><category>Mali</category><description>At a Koulikoro awareness day on Tuesday 16 November, participants paid the regional and local development tax in the presence of municipal authorities.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:54:09 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" length="29829" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ml.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
